        "original_id": "dc0d3199-2610-55a9-aa83-efd9d033127b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Robinsons, Pocari Sweat, Robinsons barley water\n- Companies: Britvic, Otsuka Pharmaceutical\n- People: Hugh Manning, Kathleen Harrison\n- Places: England, Japan, East Asia, Southeast Asia, Middle East\n- Roles: Butler\n- Works: Mrs Thursday\n- Topics: drink brands, sports drinks, television commercials\n\nFacts:\n- Robinsons is an English fruit drink brand owned by Britvic.\n- Pocari Sweat is a Japanese sports drink manufactured by Otsuka Pharmaceutical.\n- Pocari Sweat was launched in 1980 and is available in East Asia, Southeast Asia, and the Middle East.\n- In 1966, Hugh Manning starred in the television series \"Mrs Thursday\" alongside Kathleen Harrison.\n- In \"Mrs Thursday,\" Hugh Manning played a suave and imperturbable Butler.\n- Hugh Manning’s Butler character was also used in popular television commercials endorsing the qualities of Robinsons barley water.",
